#X text 20 20 The mode bus is read directly \, so each surface decides what a page looks like. The page arrives as the selector \, a single atom \, and goes to the Lua as page <name>. g_grid.lua paints it \, and paints nothing it does not know \, so the grid goes dark on a page with no cells rather than keeping the last page., f 58;
