#X obj 1800 640 array set \$0-rgb;
#X text 20 1000 t f b b fires right to left: the type \, then the index \, then the color \, so a spec's bytes cannot swap. An RGB color reads its three bytes red first: t f f f fires right to left too., f 40;
#X text 1800 760 The RGB entries \, three bytes each \, 0 to 127: the drum page's eight velocity levels at full brightness \, white for level 1 falling evenly to red for level 8 \, then the same eight at a quarter \, then a drum pad not selected \, bright pink \, then a bar's first step \, blue \, and a repeat pad or the 500 BPM repeat \, the brightest purple \, and whiter when held \, then the selected drum pad \, red \, then the edges' section green \, dim and full \, and revert's gray \, then a drum pad whose track won't play \, muted or left out of a solo \, pink at a quarter \, and the same selected \, red at a quarter \, then the saved tempo's pad \, dim blue and bright when held \, then the eight rows' voices \, each full and at a quarter \, then a fader's eight levels \, green up to red \, full and at a quarter \, and a knob's blue \, full and at a quarter. g_grid writes 128 + k to the surface for entry k., f 50;
